{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>If now I have found favor in Your eyes, HaShem — let HaShem now go in our midst.</b> Both in alef-da'at (i.e., אדני). <b>For it is a stiff-necked people.</b> You said: 'For I will not go up in your midst, for it is a stiff-necked people.' On the contrary — precisely because it is a stiff-necked people, I ask that You go in our midst. Another interpretation: <b>for it is a stiff-necked people</b> — even though <b>it is a stiff-necked people</b>, like 'and pardon my iniquity, for it is great.' Why do I ask that You go in our midst and pardon our iniquity? Since an angel has no authority to pardon, as it is written: 'for he will not bear your transgression.' And the people is stiff-necked and sins; it is better that You go and pardon each one immediately." "<b>And our heritage.</b> And You shall give us as heritage the land that You swore — like 'these are the heads of the fathers' houses who shall give as heritage (ינחלו) to the children of Israel,' which is like ינחילו (cause to inherit)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:48.056914493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}